From 2f450e2810461a5e1e26820463df4dbac43cc92d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yago Lasse <yagolasse@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:32:53 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] apu: atomic FE decode for the ISR, wait for locked voices,
 drop detector

DirectSound frees the voice named in FEDECPARAM when FEDECMETH says
"idle voice" (0x8000). Its ISR reads the two registers one after the
other, and here it runs on the frame thread while game threads keep
issuing FE methods: it read METH = 0x8000 left from a trap and PARAM =
the voice the game had just selected, and freed a playing voice (MKSM's
level music). A FEDECMETH read now snapshots both under the device lock,
and the same thread's next FEDECPARAM read returns the matching half.

Also, closer to the hardware's serial front end:
- guest FE methods run under the device lock; FEDEC is frozen while the
  FE is trapped; only one idle-voice trap at a time
- the voice-list walk waits for a title-locked voice (VOICE_LOCK) like
  xemu's voice_work_dispatch, capped at 20 ms (then skips the voice)

Diagnostics (RECOMP_APU_STATS): voice on/off, SSL stream and lock-wait
counters in [APU-STATS]; =2 adds per-voice [APU-VOICE] lines;
[APU-DROP] reports a voice still active that fell off every list, with
the last FE methods and register events; [APU-TOP] logs title writes of
the 2D list top with FEDEC and the host call stack.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016ahYm8JBvCH5KhgtSu9Yoy
